<title>USA: Senate panel approves U.S. shipping bill.</title>
<headline>Senate panel approves U.S. shipping bill.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Senate Commerce Committee Thursday approved a bill to reform the shipping tariff filing system and promote competition among common carriers.</p>
<p>The bill would end the requirement that common carriers file tariffs with the government and allow tariffs to be made available by private publication including the Internet.</p>
<p>It would also allow common carriers who do not operate vessels to enter into service contracts as carriers and transfer the functions of the Federal Maritime Commission to the Intermodal Transportation Board. The bill passed 20-0 and was sent to the full Senate.</p>
</text>
